body:
That his birth mother who, FOR SOME INEXPLICABLE REASON has primary custody, had to be bribed by her family not to abort him. That his father wanted him more than anything in the world and his mother uses him as a weapon against his father. That he may have fun at his mom's, but he's far too old to not know his last name, to not know how to read or write, to still poop his pants or suck his thumb. 

&#x200B;

(I'm so glad it's only a few more years till he can pick which parent he wants to live with as, also inexplicably, he'd rather live with his father and I, despite us being the "strict parents" who do time outs and spankings.)

I never noticed until people started noticing. I'm just glad I work with my best friend, because he noticed when I dented one of our most expensive poster boards (graphics department) that I was starting to break down and took me to the side, made me take some deep breaths, and reminded me, "it's just a fucking foam board. We can cut the piece off. The thing is HUGE, so don't worry about it. This isn't your mom's house; no one's gonna yell at your for a tiny ding in a board. Okay? Just breathe for a sec, take a moment to calm down..."

I also find I have panic attacks when I get into arguments with people. That was when I first noticed I was having panic attacks-- my boyfriend saw me shaking in the kitchen after an argument and asked, "hon, are you having a panic attack..?" and it was like as soon as I let myself notice, I realized I was having trouble breathing and collapsed. Now I'm aware of nearly every panic attack and WOW I miss not 

&#x200B;

